  "body": "By my reading of the [[Set]] algorithm for legacy platform objects (https://heycam.github.io/webidl/#legacy-platform-object-set), it seems to state that an interface that doesn't support indexed properties, but does support named properties, will not allow setting indexed properties (by way of conversion to DOMString). (See step 1.2).\r\n\r\nAt the same time, the Storage interface (https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webstorage.html#the-storage-interface) only supports named properties, so as per my understanding, something like:\r\n\r\n`window.localStorate[7] = \"foo\";`\r\n\r\nshould not be allowed. But, browsers (I tested Safari and Firefox) do allow this.",
